%20proxy'%3F%20The%20new%20term%20for%20coworkers%20who%20blindly%20share%20AI%20output%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%226720%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22A%20cooler%20full%20of%20meat%20is%20pictured.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a8da9bf3f7df8787cff3088%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%224480%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EHave%20a%20coworker%20who%20keeps%20sending%20messages%20straight%20from%20ChatGPT%3F%20They%20might%20be%20a%20%26quot%3Bmeat%20proxy.%26quot%3B%3Cp%3EKilito%20Chan%2FGetty%20Images%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3E%26quot%3BMeat%20proxy%26quot%3B%20refers%20to%20someone%20who%20sends%20outputs%20straight%20from%20Claude%20or%20ChatGPT%20without%20analyzing%20them.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EIt%20was%20popularized%20by%20Niklas%20Gruhn%2C%20a%20German%20software%20engineer.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3ETechies%20on%20X%20are%20using%20the%20term%20%26quot%3Bmeat%20proxy%26quot%3B%20to%20call%20out%20developers%20who%20ship%20%3Ca%20data-autoaffiliated%3D%5C%22false%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fai-writing-all-startup-code-thats-creating-a-new-problem-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eunreviewed%20AI%20code%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EYour%20AI-pilled%20coworker%20is%20getting%20a%20bit%E2%80%A6%20meaty.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMany%20office%20workers%20know%20what%20it's%20like%20to%20be%20inundated%20with%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fworkslop-oozing-americas-white-collar-offices-generative-ai-2025-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eunreviewed%20AI%20outputs%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Maybe%20you%20have%20a%20coworker%20who%20pastes%20messages%20from%20ChatGPT%20right%20into%20Slack.%20Maybe%20your%20manager%20keeps%20using%20too%20many%20em-dashes%2C%20or%20your%20direct%20report%20can't%20explain%20the%20code%20they%20just%20shipped.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThere's%20a%20new%20word%20for%20these%20AI%20users%3A%20%26quot%3Bmeat%20proxy.%26quot%3B%3