s.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EUS%20Air%20Force%20medics%20are%20learning%20how%20to%20treat%20and%20evacuate%20patients%20as%20drones%20threaten%20field%20care%20operations%20and%20hospitals%2C%20confronting%20an%20emerging%20threat%20for%20which%20their%20traditional%20medical%20training%20hasn't%20prepared%20them.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BDrones%20are%20a%20very%20real%20threat%2C%20and%20our%20medical%20Airmen%20are%20not%20prepared%20through%20their%20typical%20medical%20training%20to%20handle%20these%20UAVs%2C%26quot%3B%20Maj.%20Sarah%20Blackthorne%2C%20an%20Air%20Force%20medical%20planner%20involved%20in%20the%20training%2C%20said%20in%20a%20military%20news%20release.%20%26quot%3BWe%20developed%20a%20drone%20stress%20inoculation%20event%20testing%20how%20they%20might%20evacuate%20a%20field%20hospital.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EDuring%20the%20Northern%20Strike%20exercise%20in%20Michigan%20this%20month%2C%20active-duty%20Air%20Force%20and%20National%20Guard%20medics%20faced%20a%20simulated%20drone%20attack%20on%20a%20field%20hospital.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ETroops%20strung%20up%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fukraine-lined-nets-drones-cover-length-florida-warfare-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eanti-drone%20netting%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20a%20common%20tool%20on%20Ukrainian%20battlefields%2C%20and%20used%20small-arms%20fire%20to%20counter%20uncrewed%20aircraft.%20They%20used%20an%20uncrewed%20ground%20robot%20to%20inspect%20downed%20enemy%20drones%20and%20then%20moved%20patients%20to%20an%20underground%20medical%20facility%2C%20moving%20beneath%20anti-drone%20netting%20for%20protection%20along%20the%20way.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ENear%20the%20front%20lines%20in%20Ukraine%2C%20anti-drone%20netting%20can%20often%20be%20seen%20covering%20supply%20routes%2C%20troops%20are%20pushing%20support%20infrastructure%20like%20field%20hospitals%20underground%2C%20and%20uncrewed%20ground%20vehicles%20are%20becoming%20increasingly%20common%20for%20dangerous%20medical%20and%20logistics%20operations.%20%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EDefeating%20drones%20remains%20a%20challenge.%20Those%20that%20break%20through%20electronic%20warfare%20defenses%20may%20leave%20troops%20scrambling%20to%20fend%20them%20off%20with%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fukraine-soldiers-best-chance-russia-fiber-optic-drones-shotguns-2025-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Elittle%20more%20than%20a%20shotgun%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20solutions%20are%20limited%20for%20countering%20these%20threats%20en%20masse.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUS%20training%20planners%20sought%20to%20replicate%20some%20of%20the%20conditions%20confronting%20medical%20teams%20in%20Ukraine.%20The%20US%20medics%20worked%20from%20a%20Cold%20War-era%20underground%20bunker%20meant%20to%20mimic%20the%20hardened%20sites%20Ukrainian%20medical%20teams%20often%20use%2C%20Blackthorne%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20Ukraine%2C%20medical%20facilities%20are%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fukraine-zero-line-dangerous-soldiers-wait-week-run-meters-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Etargeted%20by%20aerial%20drones%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20rendering%20tents%20or%20other%20unprotected%20sites%20vulnerable.%20Hardened%20or%20underground%20facilities%20come%20with%20their%20own%20strains%20though%2C%20as%20medical%20teams%20are%20forced%20to%20contend%20with%20limited%20power%20and%20lighting%2C%20the%20shocks%20of%20nearby%20explosions%2C%20limited%20supplies%2C%20and%20logistics%20chains%20constricted%20by%20drone%20attacks.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BWe%20don't%20want%20it%20to%20be%20the%20first%20time%20they%20experience%20UAVs%20on%20deployment%2C%26quot%3B%20Blackthorne%20said.%20%26quot%3BOpportunities%20to%20get%20exposure%20here%20to%20those%20things%2C%20where%20they%20can%20work%20through%20the%20stress%2C%20are%20valuable.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20recemt%20exercise%20reflects%20a%20major%20shift%20from%20the%20kind%20of%20medical%20operations%20the%20US%20military%20grew%20accustomed%20to%20during%20two%20decades%20of%20war%20in%20Iraq%20and%20Afghanistan.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUS%20combat%20medics%20have%20long%20been%20trained%20to%20operate%20alongside%20other%20troops.%20Navy%20corpsmen%2C%20for%20instance%2C%20have%20long%20fought%20alongside%20Marine%20Corps%20infantry%20platoons.%20However%2C%20the%20vast%20majority%20of%20the%20military's%20medical%20system%20spent%20the%20Global%20War%20on%20Terror%20operating%20under%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fnext-war-may-leave-wounded-troops-waiting-weeks-for-evacuation-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Edramatically%20different%20conditions%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Wounded%20troops%20were%20usually%20quickly%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-warned-golden-hour-save-soldiers-threatened-russia-ukraine-lost-2024-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eevacuated%20from%20battlefields%3C%2Fa%3E%20to%20medical%20facilities%20on%20large%20bases%2C%20fortified%20against%20gunfire%20and%20improvised%20explosive%20device%20blasts.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20a%20future%20fight%20against%20a%20drone-capable%20adversary%2C%20such%20evacuation%20may%20not%20be%20an%20option.%20Stockpiles%20of%20cheap%20drones%20could%20threaten%20not%20just%20troops%20fighting%20on%20the%20front%20lines%2C%20but%20also%20medical%20teams%2C%20treatment%20facilities%2C%20and%20supply%20and%20evacuation%20routes.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BAs%20the%20threat%20environment%20changes%2C%20we%20need%20to%20change%20as%20well%2C%20along%20with%20the%20techniques%20we%20utilize%2C%26quot%3B%20said%20Air%20Force%20Surgeon%20General%20Lt.%20Gen.%20John%20DeGoes%20of%20the%20training.%20%26quot%3BIt%20is%20important%20to%20work%20through%20these%20scenarios%20to%20not%20only%20be%20ready%20for%20the%20current%20threat%20but%20also%20be%20mentally%20ready.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsid